  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Monday)\nIssued at 1130 AM CDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nThe surface pattern will continue to be dominated buy an extensive\nsurface high centered over southeast Canada extending southwest-\nward into the Southern/Central Plains. This will keep \ntemperatures cooler than recently with a bit lower humidity, but \nlikely still above normal for daytime highs. This effect will be \nmore noticeable across northeast OK and northwest AR.\n\nAn upper level high over the region will weaken as a system moves\nthrough the plains by the weekend. This will result in an \nincrease in shower and thunderstorm chances while maintaining \ntemperatures a little above normal. At this point no major cool-\ndown is evident anytime soon.",
